# Top-level Python dependencies for the Dripito validation analysis pipeline.
#
# Hand-edit this file. Regenerate the hash-locked requirements.txt by running
# pip-compile inside a Linux container (matching the Docker base image) so
# platform-conditional deps like pexpect get pinned:
#
#     docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/work" -w /work python:3.12.7-slim-bookworm \
#         bash -c "pip install -q pip-tools && \
#                  pip-compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras --allow-unsafe \
#                              --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in"
#
# Do NOT run pip-compile on Windows — ipython's pexpect dep is Unix-only,
# pip-compile skips it on Windows, and the Linux Docker build then fails
# under --require-hashes. Always compile on Linux.
#
# Do NOT hand-edit requirements.txt — it is generated and would lose hashes.

